const rec1 = `STAGE ideation_1: selection. Read the 3 prior rounds (Frechet-successor codebook, CURVCTRL per-level curvature, LORENTZ profile smoothing, behcone, succboost-geoshift, BRANCHCURV, BRad radial assignment, TSG-SID). All of them relocate or reweight CODEBOOK POINTS / assignment weights. Unoccupied coupling position: the metric itself. Chosen: behaviour-warped Poincare distance D^2 = d_P^2*(1+rho_i), rho_i in [0,1] from a frozen trace-normalised successor covariance, used in RQ assignment and reconstruction. Behaviour-off => rho=0 (pure Poincare); geometry-off => Euclidean base with same rho. Bounded warp removes any tuning knob. Open: sign of the warp is argued from rate allocation, not measured (main risk).`;
const rec2 = `STAGE ideation_1: final answer = IDEA BEHMET-RQ (behaviour-warped Poincare metric inside RQ assignment + reconstruction). Switch flags phi_behavior (V_i:=0) and phi_geometry (Euclidean base) exist in code; only the both-on run is trained, no ablation arm, no sweep, one seed. Derived constants: c=1 fixed, r=round(sqrt(d))=8, add-alpha=1/V, trace-normalised anisotropy budget, clamp rho to [0,1]. Behaviour table frozen from training-split directed transitions only (PPMI -> rank-16 SVD -> per-item rank-8 successor covariance), so no val/test leakage. Marginal cost approx 5-8 percent per step over 72k steps plus a one-off CPU PPMI SVD. Full labelled block is in the response; main risk is that the behaviour basis is misaligned with the latent space so the warp degenerates to isotropic noise.`;
await tools.progress.append_progress({content: rec1});
await tools.progress.append_progress({content: rec2});
return "ok";

